  "body": "## Exact source subject\n\n```text\nbase branch:  integration/vnext-main-20260811\nbase commit:  e31df34dd30d046c78057eaa7af775b3210aa9b1\nbase tree:    a2744945db8d98bef43a00205c939e2f1986b80b\nrestore commit: 64602c2f52e19741cc1acdd5f0f975b2645b2aea\nhead commit:  185dcaff7d610dfd5a6e3ece96c75699e8cdcb49\nhead tree:    5dec7e2f400fa53929e2a620f04d3fbd5821284b\ntopology:     two linear commits\nchanged paths: 11\n```\n\nAny movement of base/head/tree or review surface requires a fresh terminal packet and review.\n\n## Why this restoration is required\n\nThe external-evidence paths were previously published in hardened PR #456 tree `03dd11db161c7d3c55003552103cd3aa914e80b5`, but the later branch-convergence/retirement sequence left the current integration tree without `.g1/trillionnium_os_external_evidence` and without its source-only workflow. The first commit restores only the ten exact reviewed blobs onto the current integration baseline; it does not import PR #456's other 56 paths.\n\nThe second commit adds one scoped CI correction: `PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX` redirects explicit Python bytecode compilation into `runner.temp`. Run `34143305746` had already passed all substantive document, source, Cargo, test, Clippy and formatting steps, then failed only because two `.pyc` files appeared under the checkout despite `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`. This change prevents that source-tree mutation rather than deleting arbitrary untracked files after the fact.\n\n## Exact restored blobs\n\n```text\n.g1/trillionnium_os_external_evidence/EXECUTOR.md                         457903829f867765e9bffef4edd92812d0faa37e\n.g1/trillionnium_os_external_evidence/README.md                           c6d94d16464a17f09ffeaeb036c99a92bef6c81f\n.g1/trillionnium_os_external_evidence/admission_service.py                74c49a8763631766b5f699b10675549f6267dee8\n.g1/trillionnium_os_external_evidence/execution-policy.template.json      85c167ede7d4bf0fb5465797a5251f888669cbf5\n.g1/trillionnium_os_external_evidence/policy.template.json                7d795bb6fea3078580457020df01067ae5e20bf1\n.g1/trillionnium_os_external_evidence/tests/test_admission_service.py     68d2e3f221666cca69c36ae8109c76a0d9642352\n.g1/trillionnium_os_external_evidence/tests/test_trusted_executor.py      65799662608327a359436106e2338d667ce6b139\n.g1/trillionnium_os_external_evidence/trusted_executor.py                 32733f66e606770c99c354eadc6d4d42fcb2acde\n.github/workflows/rust-ci-full.yml                                         05b951df70c7fe0b1cd05bdba32432a7d16d84b1\n.github/workflows/trillionnium-os-external-evidence-source.yml            d90b51cd3e19c4df4334cd26fdd00e3685c06d95\n```\n\n## Source blockers addressed\n\n- nonblocking special-file rejection before `fstat`, with descriptor-pinned directory traversal;\n- descriptor ownership on every partial acquisition and invalid-policy path;\n- strictly positive, bounded authorization intervals;\n- case-folded role separation and policy-defined independent-approval cardinality/exclusions;\n- immutable sealed-memfd execution of the verified harness bytes;\n- exact filename/internal nonce identity;\n- authority expiry bounded through execution and bundle acceptance;\n- bounded, nonblocking bundle inspection and exact closed-world manifest fields;\n- release-mode cargo-chef prewarming in an isolated archive copy, followed by exact commit/tree/clean-checkout verification before Clippy.\n\n## Verification history and fresh gate\n\nThe restored bytes are identical to the PR #456 hardened objects. The dedicated `Trillionnium OS external-evidence source boundary` workflow passed all 26 tests at restore commit `64602c2f...`. Fresh exact-head and synthetic-merge CI is required for `185dcaff...`; historical results establish provenance only.\n\nExpected focused command:\n\n```bash\ncd .g1/trillionnium_os_external_evidence\npython3 -m py_compile admission_service.py trusted_executor.py tests/*.py\npython3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v\n```\n\n## Authority boundary\n\nThe checked-in policy templates remain deliberately unprovisioned. This PR performs no target checkout, runner allocation, target contact, device mutation, destructive fault, signing or release. It creates no L2-L6 evidence and cannot change a Trillionnium OS gap. `automatic_redispatch=false`, `promotion_authorized=false`, and `public_release=false` remain mandatory.",
